			"text": "Motlayoichthys is a ray-finned fish discovered in Muhi Quarry of Mexico, dating back to Early and maybe Late Cretaceous. Its name is a combination of 'Montlayolo' meaning decorated/ornamented in the Náhuatl language and 'ichthys' meaning fish. Its skull was around 15 centimeters long, making the full animal a rather medium sized fish."
